      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Kandinsky 6.0 Video Super-Resolution 2.0\n\nUpscales a video x2, x2.25 or x4 (tiled: KVAE encode, latent upscaler, DiT in two pi-Flow steps, KVAE decode, blend). The output keeps the source audio.\n\n**Files** (converted single files, see the pack's README):\n\n| Folder | File |\n|---|---|\n| models/diffusion_models/kandinsky-sr | kandinsky6_vsr_2.0_distilled2steps_bf16.safetensors (default, 3.2 GB), or kandinsky6_vsr_2.0_distilled2steps_int8_convrot.safetensors (2.0 GB, close to bf16) |\n| models/vae/kandinsky-sr | kandinsky_kvae_3d_2.0_t4s16_bf16.safetensors |\n| models/latent_upscale_models/kandinsky-sr | kandinsky6_sr_latent_upscaler_x2_bf16.safetensors, kandinsky6_sr_latent_upscaler_x4_bf16.safetensors |\n\nOriginal weights: [kandinskylab/Kandinsky-6.0-VSR-2.0-distilled2steps-Diffusers](https://huggingface.co/kandinskylab/Kandinsky-6.0-VSR-2.0-distilled2steps-Diffusers) (MIT).\n\n**Settings**\n- scale: 2x and 4x tile the clip into 512x768 (or 512x512) output tiles; 2.25x = 1.125x bilinear, then 2x.\n- seed 42 is the reference's default.\n- Sources above 24 fps are thinned to 24 fps. Any length: a clip longer than window_frames (361 frames, 15 s) runs in windows that share 9 frames, cross-faded where they meet; detail softens briefly at each join.\n- kernels: fast (default) or exact (the reference's arithmetic, about 2x slower).\n- stitch: pixels (default, as the reference) or latent (decodes the whole frame once: faster, a little sharper where tiles overlap).\n- second_gpu (loader, advanced): tiles on a second card too; it needs its own DiT and KVAE (about 6.5 GB more RAM).\n\n**Time** for 15 s (361 frames) on an RTX 4090: 960x540 to 1080p in 4.8 min (4.0 min with an RTX 3090 beside it); 1920x1080 to 4K in 15.7 min with both cards and stitch latent.\n\nCode: [kandinskylab/kandinsky-video-sr](https://github.com/kandinskylab/kandinsky-video-sr).\n\n\nDownload every file, already in this folder layout: [PedroMarinhoDev/Kandinsky-SR-ComfyUI](https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/Kandinsky-SR-ComfyUI)."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Kandinsky 6.0 Video Super-Resolution 2.0\n\nUpscales a video x2, x2.25 or x4 (tiled: KVAE encode, latent upscaler, DiT in two pi-Flow steps, KVAE decode, Hann blend). The output keeps the source audio.\n\n**Files** (converted single files, see the pack's README):\n\n| Folder | File |\n|---|---|\n| models/diffusion_models/kandinsky-sr | kandinsky6_vsr_2.0_distilled2steps_bf16.safetensors |\n| models/vae/kandinsky-sr | kandinsky_kvae_3d_2.0_t4s16_bf16.safetensors |\n| models/latent_upscale_models/kandinsky-sr | kandinsky6_sr_latent_upscaler_x2_bf16.safetensors, kandinsky6_sr_latent_upscaler_x4_bf16.safetensors |\n\nOriginal weights: [kandinskylab/Kandinsky-6.0-VSR-2.0-distilled2steps-Diffusers](https://huggingface.co/kandinskylab/Kandinsky-6.0-VSR-2.0-distilled2steps-Diffusers) (MIT).\n\n**Settings**\n- scale: 2x and 4x tile the clip into 512x768 (or 512x512) output tiles; 2.25x = 1.125x bilinear, then 2x.\n- seed 42 is the reference's default; tile i uses seed + i.\n- Sources above 24 fps are thinned to 24 fps; at most 361 frames (15 s) are upscaled.\n- Time grows with the tile count: 768x512 at 2x is 9 tiles, at 4x 25 tiles.\n\nCode: [kandinskylab/kandinsky-video-sr](https://github.com/kandinskylab/kandinsky-video-sr).\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
